# Contabo database access

When the user asks how to add or run SQL on the server database, give these commands. Always connect as `creativecloud`. Never use the `inspect360` database user to run migrations (it is not the table owner). Do not tell them to run `npx tsx` on the server; the app source is not checked out there.

SSH to the Contabo host, then:

Development (`inspect360_dev`, prompt must be `inspect360_dev=#`):

```bash
docker exec -it postgres psql -U creativecloud -d inspect360_dev
```

Production (`inspect360`, prompt must be `inspect360=#`):

```bash
docker exec -it postgres psql -U creativecloud -d inspect360
```

The app itself still connects as user `inspect360`. After creating a new table as `creativecloud`, grant that user access:

```sql
GRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE ON <table_name> TO inspect360;
```
